# Do not reference fork PRs

Do not mention, link, or number a `metatensor/<repo>#<n>` pull request (or a `github.com/metatensor/.../pull/<n>` URL) when that PR was opened from one of Eric's forks (`EricBoittier/...`).

GitHub turns those references into backlinks and notifications. That noise is unwanted.

Eric adds the link himself when he wants it. Describe the change without the PR number.

This applies to commits, PR and issue text, review comments, code comments, and docs. Reading a PR with `gh` is fine. Posting anything to GitHub still requires an explicit ask in the moment.
